@page "/docs/components/skeleton"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Skeleton
<PageTitle>Skeleton - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Skeleton</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="skeleton" />
        </div>
        <p>A placeholder block you size and shape with classes to match the content that is still loading. Its default sweep is the <a class="text-foreground font-medium" href="docs/utilities/shimmer">Shimmer</a> utility in its surface mode, so <code>shimmer-duration-*</code> and the other shimmer utilities tune it here too. The animation respects the reduced-motion setting of the operating system or browser.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(SkeletonUsageExample)" />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default" Example="typeof(SkeletonDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Animations" Description="`Animation` switches between the default `Shimmer` sweep, an opacity `Pulse`, and `None` for a static block." Example="typeof(SkeletonAnimationsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Card" Example="typeof(SkeletonCardExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="A skeleton is a plain element, so `Class` sets its size, shape and tint. This example uses indigo blocks with the `Pulse` animation."
          Example="typeof(SkeletonCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the avatar block moves to the right and the text lines line up beside it." Example="typeof(SkeletonRtlExample)" />
</div>

